                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1819"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>At Ed Pope comments, while there is 'no reason to suppose the mrs W at
                            King's to be the same as mrs W at Carlisle's 10 years later, but they
                            could all be Bonne Wilson (nee Boileau) died Feb 1819 who married at
                            Madras 1780 Lestock Wilson (died 1821) captain in East India Company's
                            service, friend of Joseph Farington and appeared often in Farington
                            diary. The Morses and the Greens brothers and sisters in law of
                            Nathaniel Middleton were part of their circle. Her husband would have
                            been frequently away sailing to India and back. </p>
